{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>לנפשי</b> — on account of my soul, like the way: ויאמר פרעה לבני ישראל, say to me, is he my brother." "<b>ישועתה</b> — two [signs] mark it as feminine by way of elegance, like אימתה בצרתה. And he attached 'to him' upon his soul, like להריק נפש רעב." "<b>Many interpret</b> סלה — like לנצח, and it is not correct. And the translator of the Book of Psalms to others [i.e., into Arabic] said: for the word סלה has no meaning, only it is for adjusting the sense of the melody. And the proof is that this word is not found in all of Scripture, except in the prayer of Habakkuk three times, which is like the manner of Psalms upon shigyonot, like: שגיון לדוד למנצח בנגינותי. And behold, the meaning of סלה would be לנצח, and it is written על מי מריבה סלה. And once it was also written: וקדוש מהר פארן סלה." "<b>And some say</b> that סלה — שב אל וקדוש. And furthermore it is written: ערות יסוד עד צואר סלה. And the correct interpretation is that the meaning of סלה is like: כן הוא, or ככה, and the matter is true and correct."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {2 "The phrase 'לאחרים אמר' is ambiguous; translated hyper-literally. It may refer to a translator rendering Psalms into another language (likely Arabic, possibly Saadia)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:13.026397104Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}